pinyon-shift-fh1-render-test-v1
# Physics oracle A/A (RF-5, docs/REIMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md RI-0.5). Free
# roam on acc9-stock (stock R34) as fh1-physics-accel: wake the car, then
# full throttle from frame 1100 until 2700 at a fixed 60 Hz clock (the car
# only pulls away near frame 1320). The player's body is snapshot at frame
# 1500 (about 3 s into the launch, still accelerating in a low gear) and is
# restored at 1800, 2100 and 2400, so it never drives more than 8 s; each
# window traces 240 steps. Run with
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle=true
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle_snapshot_frame=1500
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle_inject_frames=1800,2100,2400
# (add --pinyon_shift_physics_oracle_fixed_dt=0.008333333 to step the body
# with a constant dt), then compare the windows with
# tools/re/physics-inject-compare.py <output>/physics-oracle.bin.
# Each injection also records the state it replaced: the negative control.
# clock-hz 60
input 0 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 360 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 375 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 480 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 495 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 600 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 615 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 720 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 735 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 780 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
wait 900 3000 vehicle
capture 1090 start
input 1100 0000 0 255 0 0 0 0
capture 2700 end
input 2700 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
stop 2710
